    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Inspect the bubble wraps' quality</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Look for bubbles that are uniform in size and thickness.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Ensure ample coverage</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The bubble wraps should be sufficient to cover your vehicle's entirety, including vulnerable areas such as corners, bumpers, and wheels.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 03</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Check for any tears, punctures, or damage: Damaged bubble wraps may compromise the vehicle's safety during transportation.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<h3>Corrugated Sheets</h3>
	<p>Corrugated sheets serve as additional layers of protection for your car during transit. These sheets are made from a robust material that can absorb shock and distribute it evenly across your vehicle's surface.</p>
	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Inspect the corrugated sheets' quality and condition: Ensure they are free from cracks, tears, or any signs of wear and tear.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Check for adequate coverage: Corrugated sheets should cover your vehicle's entirety, providing a second layer of protection.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Verify thickness and durability: The corrugated sheets should be thick and sturdy enough to absorb shocks and resist bending or denting.</span></li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Edge Buffers</h3>
	<p>Edge buffers are essential for protecting your vehicle's delicate edges from scratches and dents during transportation. They serve as a cushion between your car and the corrugated sheets or wooden crates.</p>
	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Inspect edge buffers for quality: Ensure they are made of high-quality foam or rubber material.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Check for adequate coverage: Edge buffers should be placed strategically around your vehicle to protect the edges, doors, and mirrors.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Verify durability and thickness: The buffers should be thick enough to absorb impact and resist breaking.</span></li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Custom Wooden Crates</h3></div>
